<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:28:42 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Sports</category><title>FIFA rankings: France finish the year on the podium, Morocco break into the top five</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261119-fifa-rankings-france-finish-the-year-on-the-podium-morocco-break-into-the-top-five</link><description>
FIFA unveiled its final world ranking of 2026. France remain third in the world, behind Spain and Argentina. Les Bleus have now finished in the top three for the ninth consecutive year. Morocco climb two places to fifth, equalling the best-ever ranking by an African nation, previously achieved by Nigeria in 1994. Brazil drop to seventh, while Senegal remain 18th and Ivory Coast sit 28th.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e0ba6ac-e3cb-11f1-a163-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/france-9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e0ba6ac-e3cb-11f1-a163-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/france-9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e26342ec-e3cc-11f1-a764-c11f27cb4ea0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:16:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East crisis poses 'largest threat' to energy security in history, warns IEA</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-middle-east-crisis-energy-security-iea</link><description>
The International Energy Agency said on Thursday that the Middle East crisis triggered by US and Israeli strikes on Iran in February posed the “largest threat” to energy security in history. It warned that consumers were bearing more of the costs as Iran’s blockade of the Strait of Hormuz disrupted oil shipments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfcf9412-e37f-11f1-92da-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26318617092767.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfcf9412-e37f-11f1-92da-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26318617092767.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b9d06268-e3bf-11f1-a10b-a78e24423621</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:11:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfcf9412-e37f-11f1-92da-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26318617092767.jpg">© Amirhosein Khorgooi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>COP31: Vanuatu calls for UN climate summit reform, warns of backsliding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding</link><description>
Vanuatu's Environment Minister Ralph Regenvanu has called for changes to the UN climate summit process, accusing a small group of countries of blocking progress and warning that COP31 risks reversing previous commitments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8e0060-e3d0-11f1-9616-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7VU8WE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8e0060-e3d0-11f1-9616-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7VU8WE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5df44426-e3bc-11f1-be92-6d9f3ae22326</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:00:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8e0060-e3d0-11f1-9616-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7VU8WE.jpg">© Yasin Akgul, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Xi-Trump-Putin talks live: China, US and Russia leaders to hold landmark three-way meeting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-xi-trump-putin-talks-live-china-us-russia-leaders-hold-landmark-three-way-meeting</link><description>
The leaders of China, the US and Russia are set to hold a first-of-its-kind trilateral meeting on Thursday in the Chinese city of Shenzhen, on the sidelines of an APEC summit. The meeting between Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin, which Beijing said would involve "safeguarding world peace", has raised fears of a carve-up of the globe into "spheres of influence". Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9734827a-e3c9-11f1-8ccd-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T030408Z-2074341856-RC2RQOAJQ487-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9734827a-e3c9-11f1-8ccd-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T030408Z-2074341856-RC2RQOAJQ487-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff3b55a4-e38f-11f1-829a-0dfdbe55b740</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:47:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9734827a-e3c9-11f1-8ccd-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T030408Z-2074341856-RC2RQOAJQ487-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg">© Sergei Bobylyov, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>24-month matured Comté crowned world’s best cheese</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-24-month-matured-comt%C3%A9-crowned-world-s-best-cheese</link><description>
With its nutty flavour and smooth, supple texture, it was aged for two years in a former military fortress in eastern France. Comté, an unpasteurised cow’s milk cheese from the Jura Mountains, has beaten more than five thousand challengers to the top prize at the prestigious annual 'World Cheese Awards'. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington has the story.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1cb81224-e396-11f1-bbfa-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261118-221442-221615-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1cb81224-e396-11f1-bbfa-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261118-221442-221615-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2270dff2-e396-11f1-87b3-8b1d88fc9324</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:32:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Inside Limoges City Hall devastated by arson attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261118-inside-limoges-city-hall-devastated-by-arson-attack</link><description>
Work is underway to restore the city hall of Limoges, in central France, which was devastated by an arson attack during riots on October 17. More than €1.7 million has been raised through an online fundraising campaign in the wake of the disaster. Also on the show, the highly anticipated Grand Theft Auto VI has finally been released, with gamers in Oceania among the first to get a taste of the latest instalment in the video game franchise.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a034574a-e39e-11f1-bfdd-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-fa1f6e70.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a034574a-e39e-11f1-bfdd-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-fa1f6e70.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6abb7c10-e39e-11f1-b18a-73c01f9d8f47</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:23:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Crimea bridge strike: Fact-checking fake videos of damage after Ukraine's attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261118-crimea-bridge-strike-fact-checking-fake-videos-of-damage-after-ukraine-s-attack</link><description>
Ukraine struck the Kerch Bridge linking Russia to occupied Crimea, but not all the dramatic footage circulating online is real. Multiple AI-generated videos falsely show the bridge collapsed with extensive damage. Some even used branding resembling a Ukrainian news agency to appear credible. While the bridge was indeed struck and damaged, the viral videos were fabricated using AI, as Vedika Bahl explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5b1bea-e39a-11f1-83bd-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/kerch.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5b1bea-e39a-11f1-83bd-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/kerch.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ed05ade-e39a-11f1-8df1-35772d82a0de</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:51:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Bassirou Diomaye Faye excluded from Senegal's ruling party</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bassirou-diomaye-faye-excluded-from-senegal-s-ruling-party</link><description>
In tonight's edition, the political divorce between Senegal's president and the powerful former prime minister and mentor is official. Also, all of Nigeria's states have shown willingness for a push to create their own police forces. And  in parts of the continent, conflict and a drop in funding have placed huge pressures on children's learning. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99dabb00-e394-11f1-9448-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/DL00006190-VOD-00023669-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99dabb00-e394-11f1-9448-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/DL00006190-VOD-00023669-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">10fc3a7e-e395-11f1-8fb8-2356d0896181</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:21:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Reconstruction begins at Limoges City Hall after devastating fire</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/reconstruction-begins-at-limoges-city-hall-after-devastating-fire</link><description>
It's been a month since the nationwide protests that degenerated in violence across France. The dramatic pictures of the historic City Hall in the French city of Limoges set on fire made headlines worldwide. To the relief of many, the reconstruction work on the building has now begun. Since the fire, donations have poured in and already about 80 percent of the necessary funding has been secured. FRANCE 24's Caitlin Brown reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b54e79a-cbfc-11f1-a1af-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3LR764-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b54e79a-cbfc-11f1-a1af-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3LR764-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8432f08e-e38e-11f1-a923-f10e58d8b867</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:31:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Democrats nominate Jeffries to be first Black House speaker</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-democrats-nominate-jeffries-to-be-first-black-house-speaker</link><description>
Hakeem Jeffries is on the cusp of becoming the first Black speaker of the US House of Representatives after Democrats elected him their leader Wednesday following a sweeping midterm election triumph. Jeffries faced no declared challenger, although opposition from some newly elected progressives had exposed divisions over how Democrats should wield their newfound power. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a8e4f9b8-e389-11f1-908f-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261118-204203-204553-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a8e4f9b8-e389-11f1-908f-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261118-204203-204553-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b26f4a42-e389-11f1-8f7f-376a02f98822</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:58:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli army launches ground operation in Hamas-controlled area of Gaza</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-in-hamas-controlled-area-of-gaza</link><description>
The Israeli military said it had launched an operation on Wednesday in a Hamas-controlled area of central Gaza, where an AFP journalist saw Israeli tanks position themselves east of the Nuseirat refugee camp. The rare ground operation comes after inconclusive Israeli elections, with the opposition's Gadi Eisenkot trying to form a government without caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who has built his brand on saying he will ensure Israel's security. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c27f5ac4-e368-11f1-97ec-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321586490001.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c27f5ac4-e368-11f1-97ec-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321586490001.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dd05d4d4-e388-11f1-b338-bba3e21069a0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:55:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Netanyahu's only 2 tickets are racism or starting a war: He stopped acting as a democratic player'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261118-netanyahu-s-only-2-tickets-are-racism-or-starting-a-war-he-stopped-acting-as-a-democratic-player</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Israeli writer and filmmaker Etgar Keret, author of "The Seven Good Years", joining us from Tel Aviv. Keret argues that Netanyahu is seeking to remain in power, at any cost, including delegitimizing Arab parties and prolonging conflict. “For him, it could be a never-ending war as long as he's in power. He has no incentive to stop it,” he warns. Keret also calls for Israelis to examine how the war in Gaza was conducted, arguing that “the media as a whole ignored the war.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/991ef9ca-e37f-11f1-b661-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261118-181737-182702-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/991ef9ca-e37f-11f1-b661-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261118-181737-182702-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9436c6a0-e388-11f1-b2a0-bb68cd9c3227</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:45:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Xi welcomes Trump: Does Nvidia scandal upend US-China AI race?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261118-xi-welcomes-trump-does-nvidia-scandal-upend-us-china-ai-race</link><description>
You can strike Jensen Huang from the guest list but good luck steering dinner conversation away from the topic in Shenzhen. The co-founder of the AI computing leader was to accompany the US president to the APEC summit before he was undone by revelations of a dalliance with a Chinese national that happened to coincide with a Singapore client's backdoor skirting of sanctions on its powerful H200 chips. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fce0ffda-e35c-11f1-91a4-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T135542Z-942132153-RC2DQOAWFQTC-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fce0ffda-e35c-11f1-91a4-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T135542Z-942132153-RC2DQOAWFQTC-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">195f4ad0-e381-11f1-987e-0fd3071eb874</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:42:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Hegseth makes surprise trip to Venezuela, renews military cooperation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-hegseth-makes-surprise-trip-to-venezuela-renews-military-cooperation</link><description>
US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth made an unannounced visit to Caracas on Wednesday, announcing a resumption of military cooperation with Venezuela and vowing to crack down on drug traffickers. The trip marks the highest-level US visit since the ouster of Nicolas Maduro in January, signalling a dramatic shift in relations between the two countries.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2904ad80-e382-11f1-9862-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/599f3f4f72051259cd9b18e30eeb84323754b49b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2904ad80-e382-11f1-9862-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/599f3f4f72051259cd9b18e30eeb84323754b49b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29af7170-e382-11f1-bd89-0528c6c2e5fa</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:59:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2904ad80-e382-11f1-9862-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/599f3f4f72051259cd9b18e30eeb84323754b49b.jpg">© Juan Barreto, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Why Ukraine keeps trying to bring down Russia's bridge to Crimea</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-why-ukraine-keeps-trying-to-bring-down-russia-s-bridge-to-crimea</link><description>
A Ukrainian drone and missile strike on Monday night brought down a stretch of the bridge linking the annexed Crimean Peninsula to Russia, potentially crippling a route long used by Moscow to move men and materiel into Crimea and the southern front. Here’s why Kyiv keeps testing its strength against an infrastructure project that has become synonymous with Russian President Vladimir Putin’s 2014 seizure of the peninsula.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b1cf78a-e374-11f1-ae39-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-17T132708Z-373589621-RC2PPOA5FXQR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-CRIMEA-SBU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b1cf78a-e374-11f1-ae39-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-17T132708Z-373589621-RC2PPOA5FXQR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-CRIMEA-SBU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f055bd98-e373-11f1-a1da-21f28020077c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:17:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b1cf78a-e374-11f1-ae39-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-17T132708Z-373589621-RC2PPOA5FXQR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-CRIMEA-SBU.jpg">© Security Service of Ukraine handout via Reuters</source><dc:creator>Paul MILLAR</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Beijing has supported Moscow but 'China understands that America is way more important than Russia'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia</link><description>
Following Xi Jinping's very friendly rare tarmac greeting for Donald Trump, Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Kerry Brown, Professor of Chinese Studies and Director of the Lau China Institute at King's College, London. Brown examines the complex relationship between the world's two largest economies, China's growing diplomatic influence and the competition over artificial intelligence.“China is the diplomatic center of the world,” says Brown, pointing to Beijing's ability to bring together leaders from Russia, the United States, Europe and elsewhere. He argues that China now has “extraordinary convening power" and significant influence over Russia. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2bed0054-e370-11f1-905e-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261118-150609-151600-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2bed0054-e370-11f1-905e-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261118-150609-151600-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">316d86b6-e370-11f1-ad2c-13c5d8f75fe6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:48:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French ex-PM Philippe pledges to slash spending, hike retirement age as Elysée bid falters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261118-french-ex-pm-philippe-pledges-to-slash-spending-hike-retirement-age-as-elys%C3%A9e-bid-falters</link><description>
Former prime minister Édouard Philippe pledged on Wednesday to slash public spending, scrap France’s statutory 35-hour workweek and raise the retirement age to 65 from the current 62.9 years as he unveiled a slew of measures aimed a staving off economic "catastrophe" for France. An early frontrunner in next year's presidential election, Philippe is now trailing rivals in opinion polls and at risk of missing out on the second-round runoff.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bccebde-e353-11f1-bf1a-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7UY3G7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bccebde-e353-11f1-bf1a-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7UY3G7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">934eb896-e370-11f1-b0bd-875c72b456e8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:16:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bccebde-e353-11f1-bf1a-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7UY3G7.jpg">© Kenzo Tribouillard, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>War in Ukraine: Is France in direct conflict with Russia?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-war-in-ukraine-is-france-in-direct-conflict-with-russia</link><description>
An investigation published by the French public radio channel RFI on November 17 revealed that a confidential mission by the French army known as "Volia" has been used for months to conceal the presence of French personnel in Ukraine. Russia was prompt to accuse France of direct involvement in the conflict. Is this true?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8cecea6e-e36a-11f1-b640-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/French-troops-Ukraine-10.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8cecea6e-e36a-11f1-b640-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/French-troops-Ukraine-10.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d1857d58-e36a-11f1-b037-f9b6f7051788</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:57:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Senate leadership challenge exposes divisions among Democrat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-senate-leadership-challenge-exposes-divisions-among-democrat</link><description>
As Democrats prepare to take control of the Senate, incumbent minority leader Chuck Schumer is facing an insurgent leadership bid from Senator Chris Van Hollen and disputes over party leadership are exposing divisions over what direction to take the Democratic party after their midterms sweep.
